# Resource Development

- Custom resources live under `resources/[gta916]/<name>/` with
  `fxmanifest.lua` (`fx_version 'cerulean'`, `game 'gta5'`), `server/` and
  `client/` script folders.
- The category folder is symlinked into the live profile, so edits are live:
  after changing a resource, restart just that resource from the txAdmin
  console (`restart gta916-core`) - no full server restart needed. New files
  or fxmanifest changes require `refresh` first.
- Server-side HTTP endpoints (like the `gta916-core` status page and
  `/health` JSON) are served via `SetHttpHandler` on the game port
  (`:30120/<resource>/...`). Keep `/health` machine-readable JSON - it is
  used for monitoring.
- Enhanced compatibility: Lua/JS natives are backward compatible, but any
  streamed asset (`.rpf`, models, maps) must be Enhanced-converted with
  Alchemist. Do not add legacy streamed assets to resources.
- Framework integration: depend on `qb-core` exports from custom resources;
  never edit the `qb-core/` submodule for GTA916-specific behavior.
- Prefix log lines with the resource name (e.g. `[gta916-core]`) so txAdmin
  console output stays scannable.
